/-- p25029 — 25:G2. The evaluation ceiling: without the local-checkability clause the one-rule system $\D_{\mathrm{tt}}$ asserts $\varphi$ outright on exhaustive evaluation. It is sound, and every true $\varphi$ has a derivation of length $\lvert \varphi\rvert$. So a truth lacks a derivation of length at most $H$ exactly when it is longer than $H$. The step-check of $\D_{\mathrm{tt}}$ costs on the order of $m^{q}$ evaluations. -/
